A `./` or `../` include is resolved against the directory of the file that writes it, not against the
loader roots, so a partial can pull its own neighbours without knowing where the chain started.
Depth three: the step body pulls `_references/rules.md`, which pulls `./deep/one.md`, which pulls
`../plain.md` back up a level.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-inc-relative
title: Include Relative
summary: Relative includes resolved against the including file.
jinja: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/_references/rules.md --
RULES-OK
{% include "./deep/one.md" %}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/_references/deep/one.md --
DEEP-ONE-OK
{% include "../plain.md" %}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/_references/plain.md --
PLAIN-OK
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inc-relative/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Only step.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

{% include "_references/rules.md" %}
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-inc-relative --step one
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
RULES-OK
DEEP-ONE-OK
PLAIN-OK



-- stderr --
